    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Common</em></p><p>This gold coin is stamped with a creature on each side, the two being famous rivals or enemies of one another—Iggwilv and Mordenkainen, for example, or Venger and Tiamat. One figure is on the “heads” side of the coin and the other on the “tails” side.</p><p>The coin has 1 charge and regains it daily at dawn. You can take a Magic action to expend the charge and toss the coin. Roll any die to see how it lands: heads on an even number, tails on an odd number. The result determines the effect:</p><p><strong>Heads.</strong> Choose one creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself. It makes a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 2d4 Psychic damage and has Disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the end of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage only.</p><p><strong>Tails.</strong> You take 1d4 Psychic damage.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-m614kcvf1sqVpa6Z\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p><em>Toss the Coin</em> dépense la charge et lance le dé (pair : face, impair : pile) ; utilisez ensuite <em>Heads</em> ou <em>Tails</em>. Le Désavantage de <em>Heads</em> est un rappel dans l’effet appliqué, à gérer à la main.</p></section>",
